ANSYS_CROSSCHECK_SECTION = section('Independent static solver comparison','The same chassis. A second solver.','<p>The primary ANSYS bare-chassis result gives <b>0.286392 mm paired closure</b> under matched 3.01048 kN opposed-patch loads: <b>0.143% above the CalculiX reference</b>. Three mesh levels and 11,448 independently read primary samples accompany the comparison.</p><figure><a href="assets/acr1/supplements/ANSYS_static_crosscheck.png"><img src="assets/acr1/supplements/ANSYS_static_crosscheck.png" alt="Native-result-derived paired closure field and the boundary profile compared with CalculiX." width="2520" height="828" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>ANSYS native-derived numerical data, plotted with Matplotlib; Y = 45 mm is the patch boundary. Matched linear-elastic bare-chassis model, not an assembled-hardware test.</figcaption></figure><p><a href="https://github.com/aaaaaaaaaaaavm/VOLLEY/blob/main/docs/ACR1_ANSYS_CROSSCHECK.md">Read the inputs, mesh sensitivity, clearance-budget effect and source data →</a></p>')

status=section('Current status','A defined computational configuration.','''<div class="grid two"><div><h3>Evaluated</h3><p>The integrated twelve-3U ACR1 architecture has editable CAD/STEP, nominal motion and custody checks, finite motor and coupled shot models, and a same-input host-assisted mission comparison.</p></div><div><h3>Subsequent development</h3><p>Instrumented hardware correlation, environment testing and payload/host qualification remain future work. Gen6 mixed-size studies have their own configuration and evidence.</p></div></div><a class="text-link" href="evidence.html#boundary">Read the methods, assumptions and evidence boundary →</a>''','status-section')
sequence='''<ol class="steps"><li><b>01 · Store & select</b><p>Twelve 4 kg 3U envelopes in two six-level banks. Restrain the inventory; select one cell.</p></li><li><b>02 · Feed & capture</b><p>A guided lead screw pushes laterally into the indexed lift. Positive custody transfers the payload and captive pallet.</p></li><li><b>03 · Dock & clear</b><p>The lift lowers to the carrier. Prove the pallet locks and withdraw the custody frame before enabling launch.</p></li><li><b>04 · Release & recover</b><p>Command a modeled 1–3 m/s shot. The payload departs; the pallet stays on the carrier through arrest and return.</p></li></ol>'''
page('index.html','Commanded CubeSat deployment',f'''<section class="hero"><div class="wrap hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">VOLLEY G5 ACR1 / integrated study</div><h1>One path.<br>Commanded<br><em>departures.</em></h1><p class="lead">A reusable electromagnetic carrier, guided payload transfer and individually commanded CubeSat release — evaluated as one integrated computational design.</p><div class="pills"><span>12 × 3U</span><span>1–3 m/s modeled commands</span><span>CAD + numerical evidence</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="evidence.html">Explore evidence</a><a class="button" href="{academic_raw}/VOLLEY_ED3_Report.pdf">Read ED3 report</a><a class="text-link" href="{source}">View source ↗</a></div></div>{fig('polish/assembly_hero.webp','ACR1 integrated assembly: two six-level banks, indexed lift and 2250 mm guide track.','CAD-derived Blender view · ACR1 home pose · all 387 represented objects present. Teal marks the selected feed/pallet path; payloads are nominal surrogates.')}<div class="hero-index"><span>01 / SYSTEM STUDY</span><span>ONE CONTROLLED CONFIGURATION</span></div></div></section>'''+section('01 / The operating cycle','Store. Transfer. Release.', '<p class="section-lead">The handling path connects fixed storage to one reusable launch carrier.</p>'+sequence+'<div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="concept.html">Inspect the physical interfaces →</a><a class="text-link" href="delivery-film.html">Watch the complete cycle →</a></div>')+section('02 / Study results','The full system changes the trade.', '''<div class="grid three"><div class="stat"><span>Modeled command range</span><strong>1–3 <small>m/s</small></strong><p>Coupled release, circuit and arrest cases; these are computational results.</p></div><div class="stat"><span>Installed device allocation</span><strong>156.557 <small>kg</small></strong><p>149.55672 kg CAD mass plus 7 kg power/control allowance. Payloads add 48 kg.</p></div><div class="stat"><span>Twelve-release mission</span><strong>24 <small>h</small></strong><p>All payloads and the retained host evaluated 24 hours after the final release.</p></div></div><div class="finding"><b>The same-input comparison matters.</b><p>The tested uniform 2 m/s family closes within the stated host authority. The ideal ground-pretrimmed spring comparator closes both studied target families; these preplanned cases establish no VOLLEY propellant or initial wet-mass advantage.</p><a href="orbital-analysis.html">Explore the mission result →</a></div>''')+section('03 / Inspect the work','Four routes into the evidence.','<div class="grid four">'+card('Geometry & custody','Native CAD/STEP, positive transfer, docking and the retained carrier pallet.','feeder-analysis.html')+card('Motor & resources','Finite geometry, moving mass, circuit behavior, energy and arrest.','evidence.html#motor')+card('Orbital delivery','Twelve synthetic full-state targets and the host-assisted spring comparison.','orbital-analysis.html')+card('Documents & reproduction','Report, source scene, figures, numerical outputs and reproduction routes.','docs.html')+'</div>')+section('04 / Configuration lineage','A revision with a clear identity.','''<div class="lineage"><div><span>ARCHIVE</span><h3>Original Gen5</h3><p>Earlier force, fit and mass findings remain dated evidence.</p></div><div><span>CURRENT STUDY</span><h3>G5 ACR1</h3><p>Corrected integrated twelve-3U configuration and dependent computational evaluation.</p></div><div><span>DEVELOPMENT</span><h3>Gen6</h3><p>Separately identified mixed-size handling studies and hardware correlation gates.</p></div></div><a class="text-link" href="updates.html">Configuration history →</a>''')+section('05 / Evidence in view','Inspect interfaces. Read the outputs.','<div class="grid two">'+fig('02_handoff_pallet_locks.jpg','Close view of the ACR1 pallet bayonet locks and engaged lift grips.','CAD-derived render · handoff state. Storage banks and fixed lift frame are hidden for access; omission list is in provenance.')+fig('MISSION_RESOURCES.png','Frozen mission comparison showing architecture fuel use under the declared host authority gates.','Computed result · G5-MISSION-01 · same target PV states, payloads, host and resource boundary. <a href="assets/acr1/MISSION_REPORT.md">Read source report</a>.')+'</div>')+status+section('The project ecosystem','A front door for each kind of work.','<div class="grid four">'+card('Main','Integrated system, operating sequence and engineering evidence.','https://github.com/aaaaaaaaaaaavm/VOLLEY','Engineering')+card('Labs','Alternative architectures, trade rationale and exploratory studies.','https://github.com/aaaaaaaaaaaavm/VOLLEY-lab','Research vault')+card('Thesis','Academic report, presentation and chapter evidence.','https://github.com/aaaaaaaaaaaavm/VOLLEY-thesis','Academic record')+card('Paper','Manuscript, methods, data and reproducibility.','https://github.com/aaaaaaaaaaaavm/VOLLEY-paper','Manuscript')+'</div>'))
page('concept.html','System and operating cycle',hero('System / G5 ACR1','Custody from cell to carrier.','The twelve-payload architecture combines fixed storage banks, guided lateral pushers, a central indexed lift and a reusable electromagnetic carrier.')+section('Operating sequence','Follow one payload.',sequence+'<div class="grid two">'+fig('03_captured_source_level.jpg','Captured 3U and captive pallet at source level five.','CAD-derived render · captured state · source level 5, payload floor Z830 mm. The lift holds the pallet.')+fig('04_clear_docked.jpg','Docked payload and carrier pallet below the withdrawn custody frame.','CAD-derived render · clear/docked state · payload floor Z46 mm, raised custody frame floor Z190 mm. The pallet stays with the carrier.')+'</div>')+section('Interfaces','Transfer authority before motion.','''<div class="grid three">'''+card('Guided feed','Each cell has a guided lead-screw drive and independent restraint. Feeding occurs during host coast.','feeder-analysis.html')+card('Dual custody','Lift grips and carrier bayonets overlap custody at the handoff. Prove the lock before releasing the other restraint.','feeder-analysis.html#custody')+card('Carrier recovery','The payload alone departs. The captive pallet remains attached during brake arrest and carrier return.','films.html#custody')+'''</div>''')+status+POLISH_MECHANISM_SECTION)
page('feeder-analysis.html','Geometry and custody',hero('Geometry / controlled motion','A continuous custody path.','Two fixed six-level cell banks feed one central Z-indexed lift and a carrier with a captive pallet. The current ACR1 arrangement carries twelve nominal 4 kg 3U payloads.')+section('Source geometry','387 native objects. One configuration.','<div class="grid two">'+fig('polish/assembly_hero.webp','Full ACR1 assembly with two storage banks.','ACR1 home · native-CAD-derived Blender render. All CAD objects present.')+fig('02_handoff_pallet_locks.jpg','ACR1 bayonet locks, feet and engaged lift grips.','ACR1 handoff · 219 objects omitted for interface visibility, all retained in the source scene. See exact omission list in <a href="assets/acr1/02_handoff_pallet_locks_provenance.json">view provenance</a>.')+'</div>')+section('Custody / interlocks','Prove the state before advancing.','''<ol class="steps" id="custody"><li><b>Retain & isolate</b><p>Keep nonselected cells restrained. Confirm the selected transfer channel and lift datum.</p></li><li><b>Capture & lower</b><p>Complete lateral transfer with positive payload/pallet custody, then index the loaded lift to the launch carrier.</p></li><li><b>Lock & withdraw</b><p>Engage carrier bayonets, prove the handoff, withdraw the lift grips and raise the custody frame clear.</p></li><li><b>Release & reset</b><p>Enable the shot only after the clear state. Arrest and return the carrier with the pallet still attached.</p></li></ol><div class="finding"><h3>Fault and isolation branch</h3><p>Detect stalled transfer → inhibit launcher → retain payload → isolate affected cell → supervised reset/recovery → verify before continuing with an eligible cell.</p><p>Modeled custody/interlock logic; physical fault-response validation is subsequent work.</p></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="films.html#custody">Watch custody & recovery</a><a class="text-link" href="'''+source+'''/verification">Inspect geometry and interlock evidence ↗</a></div>''')+section('Measured units / computational methods','See the actual profiles.',fig('feeder_transfer_profile.png','Calculated feeder transfer profile with its labeled axes and units.','Computed prescribed-motion result · ACR1 feeder sizing. The profile is an analytical command, not a hardware measurement.')+f'<a class="text-link" href="{source}/analysis">Source sizing and inputs ↗</a>')+status)
page('evidence.html','Engineering evidence',hero('Evidence / methods and sources','Trace a claim to its inputs.','The evaluated configuration is VOLLEY-G5-ACR1. Geometry, motor/circuit behavior and orbital delivery use explicitly identified models and source files.')+section('Evidence map','Four connected records.','<div class="grid two">'+card('Geometry & exchange','Eight native/STEP states, nominal assembly/motion checks and native mass properties.',source+'/cad')+card('Coupled shot & resources','Finite motor geometry, source/current/voltage model, arrest and explicit installed allocation.',source+'/analysis')+card('Host-assisted mission','Frozen synthetic target states, release recoil, continuous host arcs and native Orekit replay.','orbital-analysis.html')+card('Academic record','Exact report plus original scientific figures and controlled Blender views.','docs.html')+'</div>')+section('Motor / coupled model','Release and recovery share one energy account.','<div class="grid two" id="motor">'+fig('coupled_shot_reference.png','Coupled shot reference results showing the computed release and arrest histories.','Computed result · ACR1 coupled shot. Nominal modeled commands at 1, 2 and 3 m/s; declared assumptions and adverse cases stay with the source.')+fig('shot_energy_ledger.png','Computed shot energy ledger with component dissipation labels and units.','Computed result · same-revision electrical and mechanical accounting. No hardware efficiency measurement is inferred.')+'</div>'+f'<a class="text-link" href="{source}/analysis/COUPLED_SHOT.json">Inspect numerical cases ↗</a>')+EXTENDED_ENGINEERING_SECTION+ANSYS_CROSSCHECK_SECTION+section('Method boundary','Read each result in its declared model.','''<div id="boundary" class="grid two"><div><h3>Geometry and mechanisms</h3><p>Native solid geometry, nominal motion, interface retention and declared analytical sizing. Reference actuator envelopes and allocations are identified in the source; manufacturing and instrumented hardware correlation follow.</p><h3>Motor and release</h3><p>Finite geometry and coupled computational source/motion models. The 1–3 m/s command band is the supported study range; no hardware rating or flight capability is asserted.</p></div><div><h3>Orbital delivery</h3><p>Fixed-axis J2 point masses, synthetic preplanned full-state targets, constant inertial host force and Isp 220 s. Drag, higher gravity, attitude/plume allocation, navigation and finite exit geometry are outside the mission model.</p><h3>Numerical agreement</h3><p>Independent replay and step refinement assess numerical consistency. They do not establish physical delivery accuracy, measured reliability or payload compatibility.</p></div></div><div class="finding"><h3>Installed allocation</h3><p>149.55672 kg computed CAD mass + 7 kg power/control allowance = 156.55672 kg retained device allocation; + 48 kg payloads = 204.55672 kg loaded device. The generic wet host is 500 kg including its 20 kg fuel once, so the mission begins at 704.55672 kg.</p></div>''')+section('Provenance','Inspect the original output.','<div class="grid two">'+fig('finite_force_coefficient.png','Finite geometry force coefficient versus the modeled stroke.','Computed result · ACR1 finite motor model. Read axes and units at full size.')+fig('magnetic_gap_section.png','Scientific section of the magnetic gap and conductor geometry.','Scientific section · controlled ACR1 geometry. Source defines the materials and dimensional assumptions.')+'</div><p><a href="assets/acr1/ASSET_REGISTER.json">Asset register</a> · <a href="assets/acr1/VIEW_PROVENANCE.json">CAD view source hashes and camera settings</a></p>'))
mission_intro=hero('G5-MISSION-01 / twelve releases','Host assistance is part of delivery.','The same-input comparison carries twelve 4 kg 3U payloads from a nominal 500 km sun-synchronous orbit. Synthetic full-state targets are frozen before either architecture is planned.')
page('orbital-analysis.html','Host-assisted mission',mission_intro+section('Common boundary','Twelve departures. One evaluation epoch.','''<div class="grid three"><div class="stat"><span>Release schedule</span><strong>450–5400 <small>s</small></strong><p>Twelve releases, every 450 s, within the nominal 5676.978 s orbital period.</p></div><div class="stat"><span>Evaluation epoch</span><strong>91800 <small>s</small></strong><p>24 h after final release. Compare all twelve payloads and retained host at this epoch.</p></div><div class="stat"><span>Host authority gates</span><strong>1 / 5 <small>N</small></strong><p>Constant inertial resultant force; 500 kg initial wet bus; Isp 220 s.</p></div></div>'''+fig('MISSION_TARGETS.png','Frozen uniform and alternating full-state target family figure.','Computed targets · fixed-axis J2 model · uniform synthetic 2 m/s and alternating 1/3 m/s along-track target families. Targets are not customer requirements.'))+section('Result / bounded policies','The comparator closes the trade.','''<div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Fuel used by lowest-fuel feasible tested policy (kg)</caption><thead><tr><th>Target / authority</th><th>ACR1</th><th>Fixed 2 m/s spring</th><th>Ground-pretrimmed spring</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Uniform 2 / 1 N</th><td>0.052443</td><td>0.046957</td><td>0.052443</td></tr><tr><th>Uniform 2 / 5 N</th><td>0.052443</td><td>0.046957</td><td>0.052443</td></tr><tr><th>Alternating 1/3 / 1 N</th><td>No tested pass</td><td>No tested pass</td><td>0.075002</td></tr><tr><th>Alternating 1/3 / 5 N</th><td>0.289874</td><td>No tested pass</td><td>0.053645</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The ideal ground-pretrimmed spring closes both target families at either authority gate. These preplanned cases establish no Gen5 propellant or initial wet-mass advantage. A failed sampled policy is not a global infeasibility proof.</p><p>ACR1 begins at 704.55672 kg against the declared 620 kg spring case, a retained-device penalty of 84.55672 kg. The spring allocation is a class-study assumption of 12 × 6 kg.</p>'''+fig('MISSION_RESOURCES.png','Fuel and mass comparison from frozen selected candidate outputs.','Computed result · same inputs and full-state targets; fixed 20 kg host fuel budget. <a href="assets/acr1/MISSION_RESULTS.csv">Download table (CSV)</a>.'))+section('The release model','A commanded sled speed is one contribution.','''<div class="grid two"><div><h3>Host manoeuvre → pointing → release</h3><p>The host supplies the planned pre-release state and direction. The launcher adds its coupled release contribution; its retained sled recoil is recomputed at each release. The host then recovers to the common chief trajectory at one orbital period.</p><p>Gen5 reserves a 400 s zero-force loading coast for each payload, enclosing the declared 355 s mechanism cycle. Both architectures retain 5 s pre-release and 20 s post-release zero-force guards.</p></div><div><h3>Coast → modeled target state</h3><p>Each released full six-state is propagated under fixed-axis J2 to the common epoch. Material altitude or plane changes are never attributed to the launcher alone. These are generic-host synthetic delivery studies.</p><p>All targets were known before the spring energy table was fixed. The study does not establish a unique inflight-retasking benefit.</p></div></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="orbit-explorer.html">Inspect source trajectory</a><a class="button" href="films.html#mission">Watch the mission film</a></div>''')+section('Native replay','Numerical agreement has a precise meaning.',fig('MISSION_NATIVE_AGREEMENT.png','Native Orekit replay and numerical refinement agreement figure.','Computed numerical agreement · Orekit 13.1.6 / Hipparchus 4.0.3. Maximum payload target difference 1.12472029 × 10⁻⁵ m / 1.23467973 × 10⁻⁸ m/s; this is not physical accuracy.')+'<p>Point masses, fixed-axis J2, constant inertial force and Isp 220 s. Drag, higher gravity, third bodies, attitude, plume allocation, navigation and finite exit geometry are outside the model.</p><p><a href="assets/acr1/MISSION_REPORT.md">Full mission report</a> · <a href="assets/acr1/NATIVE_REPLAY_CHECKS.json">Native checks</a> · <a href="evidence.html#boundary">Evidence boundary</a></p>')+PARTIAL_MISSION_NOTE)
